  "text": {
    "id": {
      "title": "Linked list",
      "story": "Buat class `LinkedList` berupa rantai node `{ value, next }`. Jangan menyimpan elemen di array.\nMetode: `size()`, `isEmpty()`, `valueAt(i)`, `pushFront(v)`, `popFront()`, `pushBack(v)`, `popBack()`, `insert(i, v)` yang menyisipkan supaya `v` berada di indeks `i`, `erase(i)`, `reverse()` yang membalik urutan di tempat, dan `toArray()` untuk melihat isinya.\nIndeks di luar batas melempar error. `insert` boleh memakai `i` sama dengan `size()` untuk menambah di akhir. `popFront` dan `popBack` saat kosong juga melempar error.",
      "hint1": "Simpan `head`, `tail`, dan jumlah node. Banyak bug muncul saat list berubah dari kosong ke satu elemen atau sebaliknya, jadi perbarui `tail` dengan hati-hati.",
      "hint2": "Untuk `reverse`, jalan dari depan sambil membalik arah `next` setiap node. Kamu butuh tiga variabel: node sebelumnya, node sekarang, dan node berikutnya."
    },
    "en": {
      "title": "Linked list",
      "story": "Build a `LinkedList` class as a chain of `{ value, next }` nodes. Don't keep the elements in an array.\nMethods: `size()`, `isEmpty()`, `valueAt(i)`, `pushFront(v)`, `popFront()`, `pushBack(v)`, `popBack()`, `insert(i, v)` which inserts so that `v` ends up at index `i`, `erase(i)`, `reverse()` which reverses the list in place, and `toArray()` to see its contents.\nAn index out of range throws an error. `insert` accepts `i` equal to `size()` to add at the end. `popFront` and `popBack` on an empty list throw too.",
      "hint1": "Keep a `head`, a `tail`, and a node count. Many bugs show up when the list goes from empty to one element or back, so update `tail` carefully.",
      "hint2": "For `reverse`, walk from the front and flip each node's `next`. You need three variables: the previous node, the current one, and the next one."
    }
  },
